-- DOES ANY OF THIS ACTUALLY WORK?
--
-- A bot that logs in, says what it can see, tries the things that do not need anybody else to be
-- there, and stops. Run this once before writing a bot of your own: if it gets to the end, the
-- token is right, the connection works, and the bot can speak.
--
--     polite build examples/discord/check-bot.polite
--     cd examples/discord
--     node check-bot.mjs
--
-- The token goes in a file called .env beside this one:
--
--     DISCORD_TOKEN=...
--
-- It never goes in the program, and .env is never committed.
--
-- Nothing here needs anybody to say anything. The parts that do -- hearing a message, a command
-- being used, a button being pressed -- are what hello-bot and club-bot are for.
--
-- Written in PoliteLang by Creeperdiamonds Studios.


please show ""
please show "  CHECKING A DISCORD BOT"
please show ""

please remember worked is 0
please remember failed is 0

-- 1. Logging in.
please try to:
    log in to discord with the secret called "DISCORD_TOKEN"
    change worked to worked plus 1
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  x  logging in: {what went wrong}"
    show ""
    show "  Nothing else can be tried until that works."
    show ""
    stop everything
thank you for trying
please show "  ok logging in"

-- 2. Setting a status.
please try to:
    let my status be "being checked over"
    show "  ok setting a status"
    change worked to worked plus 1
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  x  setting a status: {what went wrong}"
    change failed to failed plus 1
thank you for trying

-- 3. Offering a slash command. This is also the one that says whether the bot is in a server.
please try to:
    offer the command "polite" for "A command offered by a bot written in English"
    show "  ok offering a slash command"
    change worked to worked plus 1
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  x  offering a slash command: {what went wrong}"
    change failed to failed plus 1
thank you for trying

-- 4. Saying something out loud. Change the channel name here if yours is called something else.
please remember room is "general"
please try to:
    announce "Checking in. This is a bot written in English, in a language called PoliteLang." in the channel called room
    show "  ok speaking in #{room}"
    change worked to worked plus 1
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  x  speaking in #{room}: {what went wrong}"
    show "     (change the channel name near the bottom of check-bot.polite if yours differs)"
    change failed to failed plus 1
thank you for trying

-- 5. Changing what was just said, which proves the bot can reach its own messages.
please try to:
    correct what I said to "Checking in. Everything works. I will be quiet now."
    show "  ok correcting what it said"
    change worked to worked plus 1
otherwise if it does not work out:
    show "  x  correcting what it said: {what went wrong}"
    change failed to failed plus 1
thank you for trying

please show ""
please check if failed is 0:
    show "  All {worked} of them worked. The bot is properly connected."
    show ""
    show "  Try hello-bot next, and say hello to it."
otherwise:
    show "  {worked} worked, {failed} did not. What went wrong is printed above each one."
thank you for checking
please show ""
